course: dictionary
lesson: 13922
title: Words for teachers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lecturer is a person who teaches students at a university or college. They often give lectures, which are talks to a large group of students. «My aunt is a lecturer at the university, and she teaches biology.» The clues are university, students and teaches, so a lecturer is a kind of teacher for older students.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The lecturer gave a talk about the stars» makes sense if lecturer means a university teacher or someone giving a talk. That is a good sign that you have understood it.
explain: Be careful: the word can mean more than one thing. Anyone who gives a talk to an audience can be called a lecturer, and in stories «lecturing» someone means telling them off at length.
fact: A lecturer teaches students at a university or college.
fact: A lecture is a talk given by a lecturer, often to a big group of students.
fact: Anyone who gives a talk to an audience can be called a lecturer.
fact: In the UK, lecturer is a job title below professor; in the USA, such people are often called professors.
fact: When someone says «Stop lecturing me», they mean they are telling you off for a long time.
exercise: «My sister is a lecturer at the university in Leeds.» What is a lecturer? | A person who sells books in a shop | *A person who teaches students at a university or college | A student who lives in a flat | A driver of a big red bus
exercise: «The lecturer spoke to a hall full of listeners for an hour.» What does lecturer mean here? | *Someone giving a talk to an audience | A student who forgets their homework | A person who cooks dinner | A person who drives a bus
exercise: Mum says, «Stop lecturing me, I know I was late.» What does lecturing mean? | Sleeping during a film | Singing a song loudly | *Telling someone off at length | Teaching a class of toddlers
test: «In the USA, university teachers like this are often called professors.» What are they often called in the USA? | Students | Doctors | Lectures | *Professors
test: «Every Monday the lecturer gives a lecture on maths.» What is a lecture? | *A talk given to students | A test for students | A bag for school books | A prize at the end of term
exam: «The lecturer in the hall explained the history of Egypt, and the students took notes.» What does a lecturer do in this sentence? | *Gives a talk to students to teach them | Builds the walls of the hall | Sleeps in class | Cooks lunch for the class
